Today is Sunday.
Now it is morning.
The street is very quiet.
I go to the shop.
The shop is near my house.
There is one man there.
Who is he?
He is the shopkeeper.
I say, "Brother, namaste."
He says, "Namaste, madam."
In his shop there are many Indian sweets.
They are very colorful.
I need one box of sweets.
He gives one box.
I give two hundred rupees.
This box is for my family.
My family is in Mexico.
I go home now.
There I show one sweet to my family via video call.
